{"type":"message","id":"009b97e5","parentId":"62f66ea2","timestamp":"2026-05-20T15:32:13.872Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`/send` gives error 1101 (No domain / workers not found), while `/api/send` returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". The 1101 error for `/send` suggests the `/send` route doesn't exist as a workers route. But the `/api/send` returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" suggests the request is hitting the worker but returning a string response.\n\nLet me check if maybe the POST body needs different format, or maybe the messages are going through via `/api/send` since that doesn't error. Let me verify by checking history after posting via `/api/send` with a distinct message.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-1bbf3b26-70d8-4327-8a89-8dcf011901c6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try posting with a unique marker via /api/send to verify if it works\ncurl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"VERIFY_1530_UTC_TEST\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}' \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\"\necho \"\"\nsleep 2\n# Check if it appears in history\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=2\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); [print(m['content'][:80]) for m in d['messages'][:2]]\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1285,"output":349,"cacheRead":18080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19714,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779291122273,"responseId":"chatcmpl-be755c8e-7dfc-447b-81f4-d4661d59e0da"}}
